,title,link,text,language,family
0,Korlai Portuguese Creole - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Korlai_Portuguese_Creole,"Korlai Portuguese is an Indo-Portuguese creole based on the Portuguese language, spoken by approximately 1,000 Luso-Indian inhabitants of the Korlai (Corlaim) village at the Korlai fort, a former possession of the Portuguese in Goa and Bombay.",Korlai Portuguese Creole,Creole
1,Portuguese-based creole languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Portuguese-based_creole_languages,"Contact between the Portuguese language and native languages gave rise to many Portuguese-based pidgins, used as linguas francas throughout the Portuguese sphere of influence. In time, many of these pidgins were nativized, becoming new stable creole languages.",Korlai Portuguese Creole,Creole
2,Cross Feast Song Korlai Portuguese Creole Language..,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=LvRINWltfZ4,"Enjoy the videos and music you love, upload original content, and share it all with friends, family, and the world on YouTube.",Korlai Portuguese Creole,Creole
3,Cross Feast Song...Korlai Portuguese Creole Language...use earphone ...,https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=NBfC0u0fsJc,"Enjoy the videos and music you love, upload original content, and share it all with friends, family, and the world on YouTube.",Korlai Portuguese Creole,Creole
4,Songs of Korlai ~ Trivial Matters,https://trivialmatters.blogspot.com/2007/01/songs-of-korlai.html,"Like in Daman and Diu where a similar Portuguese Creole was once spoken, the unique Creole of Korlai is slowly fading away. During the three days I spent in Korlai last weekend, I often felt as if I were walking around in a historical preserve, not a village. Or in an Indiana Jones movie or in frontier town of some faraway colonial outpost.",Korlai Portuguese Creole,Creole
5,"Indo-Portuguese Creole Language of Korlai, Maharashtra",https://www.sahapedia.org/indo-portuguese-creole-language-korlai-maharashtra,"When people speaking one language come in contact with another dominant language and start using it for various purposes, a creole (a mother tongue formed from the contact of a European language with local languages) is formed over the period of a few generations. This module explores one such creole spoken in the tiny village of Korlai near Chaul in coastal Maharashtra.",Korlai Portuguese Creole,Creole
6,Korlai Portuguese Creole Explained,https://everything.explained.today/Korlai_Portuguese_Creole/,"Korlai Portuguese vowels are similar to the Middle Portuguese, which was spoken by Portuguese soldiers that came to the region. The sole difference being the point of articulation of the central vowel. Both Marathi and Korlai Creole Portuguese had a decline in nasal vowels and this process of denasalisation is connected for both languages.",Korlai Portuguese Creole,Creole
7,Korlai Portuguese Creole language - globalrecordings.net,https://globalrecordings.net/en/language/vkp,"Korlai Portuguese Creole language and dialect information. Audio Bible stories and lessons. Download free evangelism resources, MP3s, audio bible study tools, language/dialect information.",Korlai Portuguese Creole,Creole
8,Korlai Portuguese Creole language resources | Joshua Project,https://joshuaproject.net/languages/vkp,Korlai Portuguese Creole language resources. Listing of people groups speaking Korlai Portuguese Creole. Korlai Portuguese Creole dialects and alternate names. Bible and ministry resource availability.,Korlai Portuguese Creole,Creole
9,Korlai Creole: History and Characteristics of an Indo-Portuguese ...,https://www.sahapedia.org/korlai-creole-history-and-characteristics-indo-portuguese-language-spoken-coastal-maharashtra,"Korlai Creole is a peculiar Portuguese-Marathi language spoken in the tiny village of Korlai near Chaul, Maharashtra. It was the product of bustling trade, political dominance, social exclusion and intermingling of cultures. This overview explores the linguistic history of the language and its characteristics.",Korlai Portuguese Creole,Creole
